{
  "_comment": "Hand-authored expectations for the privacy policies of test/support/target/ash/policies.json (all data invented). Records use the Ash attribute names of the fixture's project; 'gone-' IDs name records that do not exist. Personas: logged out, u1 (no role; owns d4; team t1 whose lead is u2), u2 (owner of d1, creator of n2), u3 (admin; dangling team), u4 (every field empty). reads: per type and action, the records each persona reads and the fields it may view ('all': every attribute but the primary key); 'get' reads each record by primary key (Ash.get), 'search' runs :search, 'list' runs the primary :read without a key. filters (filter_input on :search), sorts (sort_input on :search, then id) and loads (Ash.load of a relationship) probe hidden fields and gated relationships. auto_bind / creates: whether the update or create is authorized. Checked by scripts/ash_compile_check/policies.exs in PostgreSQL through the generated policies. Written against these rows only: sorts after the auto_bind updates are not asserted.",
